        <entry key="descSpc">Statistical process control model leverages control rules for detecting anomalies.</entry>
        <entry key="descTcn">Uses a Temporal Convolutional Network to reconstruct normal sequences and scores anomalies by reconstruction error.</entry>
        <entry key="descUsad">Combines autoencoder reconstruction and adversarial training to model normal patterns and scores anomalies using reconstruction-based and discriminator-based errors.</entry>
        <entry key="descDeepAnT">Forecasts future subsequences using a CNN-based model and scores anomalies by prediction error.</entry>
        <entry key="descVaelstm">Uses a variational LSTM autoencoder to learn probabilistic reconstructions of normal sequences and scores anomalies by reconstruction error and latent distribution deviation.</entry>
        <entry key="descIforest">Uses isolation trees to model normal features and scores anomalies by ease of isolation.</entry>
        <entry key="descRrcforest">Builds a forest of random cut trees summarizing normal feature distribution and scores anomalies by measuring how much a point disrupts the tree structure.</entry>
        <entry key="descLof">Estimates local density for each windowed feature set and scores anomalies by comparing a point’s density to that of its neighbors using the Local Outlier Factor algorithm.</entry>
        <entry key="descCnnae">Reconstruct normal sequences with a CNN autoencoder and scores anomalies by reconstruction error.</entry>
        <entry key="descLstmae">Reconstruct normal sequences with an LSTM autoencoder and scores anomalies by reconstruction error.</entry>
        <entry key="descLstmf">Predicts future values using an LSTM forecaster and scores anomalies by deviation between predicted and actual values.</entry>
        <entry key="descOcsvm">Computes a boundary around normal feature patterns using One-Class SVM and scores anomalies based on their distance from this boundary.</entry>

        <entry key="bestSuitedSpc">Time series with stable mean/variance where detecting amplitude deviations, shifts, or runs beyond control limits are required.</entry>
        <entry key="bestSuitedTcn">Time series with longer-range structure, contextual anomalies, or sequence-level trends.</entry>
        <entry key="bestSuitedUsad">Time series with both point‑ and subsequence‑level anomalies, requiring robust reconstruction without overfitting.</entry>
        <entry key="bestSuitedDeepAnT">Time series with short-range repeating patterns.</entry>
        <entry key="bestSuitedVaelstm">Time series with complex, nonlinear trends and uncertainty.</entry>
        <entry key="bestSuitedIforest">Time series with anomalies that are sparse, and varied.</entry>
        <entry key="bestSuitedRrcforest">Time series with anomalies that may be subtle, context-dependent, or occur in clusters, especially when robustness to noise and irregular patterns is important.</entry>
        <entry key="bestSuitedLof">Time series with clustered features and local density variations.</entry>
        <entry key="bestSuitedCnnae">Time series with short‑range, repeating patterns and shape‑based anomalies in fixed‑length windows.</entry>
        <entry key="bestSuitedLstmae">Time series  with long-term dependencies and contextual anomalies where capturing temporal order is critical.</entry>
        <entry key="bestSuitedLstmf">Time series with long‑term temporal dependencies and contextual anomalies identifiable via forecast deviation.</entry>
        <entry key="bestSuitedOcsvm">Time series with relatively stationary behavior and compact, well‑bounded feature distributions.</entry>

        <entry key="tuningRecommendationSpc">Adjust window length to capture normal variability, method for spikes or gradual shifts and lambda for trend detection.</entry>
        <entry key="tuningRecommendationTcn">Tune number of layers and filter size first, then adjust sequence length and learning rate.</entry>
        <entry key="tuningRecommendationUsad">Adjust number of latent features first, then reconstruction loss weight, then learning rate.</entry>
        <entry key="tuningRecommendationDeepAnT">Adjust max epochs and learning rate, then adjust observation window length.</entry>
        <entry key="tuningRecommendationVaelstm">Increase latent dimension first, then max epochs, then sequence length and learning rate.</entry>
        <entry key="tuningRecommendationIforest">Increase number of learners and number of observations per learner, then window length.</entry>
        <entry key="tuningRecommendationRrcforest">Increase number of learners and number of observations per learner, then window length.</entry>
        <entry key="tuningRecommendationLof">Increase Number of Neighbors and window length, then search method and distance.</entry>
        <entry key="tuningRecommendationCnnae">Increase number of convolutional layers first, then kernel size, then batch size and learning rate.</entry>
        <entry key="tuningRecommendationLstmae">Increase LSTM hidden units first, then sequence length, then epochs and learning rate.</entry>
        <entry key="tuningRecommendationLstmf">Adjust forecast horizon first, then hidden units, then learning rate and sequence length.</entry>
        <entry key="tuningRecommendationOcsvm">Adjust window length and training iterations, then Beta and Gradient Tolerances.</entry>

